From 7681889435ebbd814395e2943959c638d6428251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baverrr <342259467+baverrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:43:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Use the RavenOS glass theme for toasts, notifications and
 dialogs

Add core/res values/raven_glass.xml with the RavenOS glass theme colors
(Midnight Aurora defaults, the same names as in Settings and SystemUI),
so a product overlay can recolor system popups with the device's theme
variant, and use it for:

- Toasts: a solid raven_surface card with the raven_glass_stroke edge,
  raven_card_radius corners and raven_fg text (also used for the text
  toasts SystemUI draws for apps).
- Dark dialogs and popup menus: background_material_dark and
  background_device_default_dark are raven_bg, the floating variants are
  raven_surface, and dark Theme.Material popup menus use the floating
  color like dialogs do.
- The dark accent: accent_material_dark, and the dark DeviceDefault
  themes now use raven_accent directly, because the LineageOS overlay
  sets accent_device_default_* (and material_deep_teal_200) with a
  higher priority than product overlays.
- Notifications and heads-up cards: the night notification background
  is raven_surface; SystemUI cards get the raven_glass_stroke edge,
  raven_card_radius corners (through android:dialogCornerRadius in
  Theme.SystemUI, since config_dialogCornerRadius is set by the
  LineageOS overlay), raven_separator dividers, raven_ripple, and a
  raven_bg shade behind them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I8705645eda68e1d070adf85314f6345f49ea3979
